.TH ELIZA 1
.SH NAME
eliza \- Weizenbaum ELIZA-style conversational program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreammachines/eliza
.RI [ script.el ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Eliza
is a work-alike of Weizenbaum's ELIZA (1966), the AI chapter of
Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
a keyword-ranked pattern match and pronoun-reflection engine, not a
research replica. It ranks whichever of a script's trigger words are
present in what was typed, decomposes the highest-ranked one against a
handful of patterns, and reflects the matched pieces back with
pronouns swapped (I/you, my/your, ...) \(em the trick that reads as
understanding without there being any.
.PP
.I Script.el
defaults to
.BR /lib/eliza/doctor.el ,
a DOCTOR-style script (Weizenbaum's own name for the persona, not a
transcription of the lost 1966 original). A script defines
.BR GREETING ,
.BR DEFAULT ,
word substitutions
.RB ( PRE
before matching,
.B POST
when reflecting a captured span), and ranked
.B KEY
words each with
.B DECOMP
patterns (literal words and
.RB `` * ''
wildcards) and
.B REASSEMBLE
reply templates.
.PP
Type a line in the entry box and press Return or
.B Send
to talk to it.
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/eliza/doctor.el
.TP
.B /lib/eliza/doctor.el
The default DOCTOR-persona script.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/dreammachines/eliza.b
.br
.B /appl/dreammachines/plugin/eliza.b
.br
.B /module/dreammachines/eliza.m
